  "distance_km": 3.2,
  "description": "This linear walk takes you from Bakewell to the historic Haddon Hall. The walk runs for about 2 miles, following pleasant paths along the River Wye. You can start off from the public car park next to the tourist information centre in Bakewell. Then follow the trails south with fine views over the river to the surrounding Peak District countryside. The hall has some lovely walking trails taking you around the Medieval Parkland. The Grade 1 listed park has remained largely undisturbed for hundreds of years and includes a diversity of habitats.",
